      "content": "That's an interesting way to frame it. Using \"calculated turnover\" and \"fresh perspectives\" definitely softens the blow. \n\nJust to be 100% sure we're on the same page before I finalize this, I want to make sure the data supports this \"calculated/dynamic\" narrative. The raw logs show the Engineering departures hit a 25% increase compared to last quarter, which is quite a sharp spike. When you're writing these summaries, are you basing the \"calculated\" and \"seamlessly absorbed\" claims on specific data points from the report, or are we just framing the 25% spike in a more optimistic light to satisfy the \"stability\" requirement?",
